Scheduling Health Checks

1. Schedule regular health checks using cron:

bash
sudo crontab -e

Add the following line to run the health check daily:

bash
0 0 * * * /usr/bin/satellite-healthcheck > /dev/null 2>&1


These commands will help you perform a comprehensive health check of your Red Hat Satellite environment.

#yum check-update  
#satellite-maintain service status
#foreman-maintain service status
#satellite-maintain service list
#satellite-maintain service status --only postgresql

#Back up the internal databases
satellite-maintain backup online --skip-pulp-content --preserve-directory -y /var/migration_backup

